WEBVTT

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:08.859
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the twenty-sixth. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:17.019
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, you're coming through. Unlike the heating in the portakabin. I've still got my coat on. Just moaning, not raising a job.</v>

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:21.199
<v Tomasz Nowak>That's your winter office package. Desk, chair, mild hypothermia.</v>

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.960
<v Sarah Okafor>Well, there's a birthday cake in the office, if that's any consolation.</v>

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.109
<v Callum Reid>Depends. Proper cake or one of those healthy ones?</v>

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:37.469
<v Sarah Okafor>Proper cake. Right, before we lose the entire meeting to that, what's already cleared?</v>

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:44.939
<v Grace Liu>I've signed off the inspection on the line 3 screw on Tuesday. That's last Tuesday, all done.</v>

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:49.450
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, that was still showing in the old notes, wasn't it?</v>

00:00:51.869 --> 00:01:00.270
<v Grace Liu>It was. And I already swapped the filter on the line one HPU yesterday. That's finished as well, not another filter job for today.</v>

00:01:01.789 --> 00:01:03.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Both historical, then.</v>

00:01:05.159 --> 00:01:12.159
<v Callum Reid>Only other thing from nights: noticed the Forklift Fleet was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down.</v>

00:01:12.989 --> 00:01:16.489
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Settled back to normal, you mean? Not still creeping up?</v>

00:01:17.849 --> 00:01:22.750
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, normal again. Just an observation from the shift, nothing ongoing being raised here.</v>

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:29.840
<v Aisha Begum>And I'm still waiting on parts for the line 3 chiller, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:01:30.969 --> 00:01:33.769
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, still outstanding. No arrival to report, unfortunately.</v>

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:39.250
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that stays blocked. Not putting work against it today.</v>

00:01:40.379 --> 00:01:45.280
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie Brennan, can you send the shift handover report round by 11am? Normal priority.</v>

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:50.730
<v Jamie Brennan>The shift handover report, yeah? Not the older weekly one?</v>

00:01:52.849 --> 00:01:56.349
<v Sarah Okafor>That's it, the shift handover report. By 11am, normal priority.</v>

00:01:57.159 --> 00:01:59.609
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, I'll send it round by 11am.</v>

00:02:00.989 --> 00:02:02.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Jamie Brennan.</v>

00:02:03.049 --> 00:02:08.300
<v Sarah Okafor>Callum, can you run the monthly fire alarm test after lunch? Normal priority on that.</v>

00:02:09.849 --> 00:02:15.099
<v Callum Reid>Yeah. Monthly test rather than an evacuation exercise, just so we're saying the same thing?</v>

00:02:16.129 --> 00:02:18.580
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly, just the monthly fire alarm test.</v>

00:02:20.719 --> 00:02:23.520
<v Callum Reid>Fine, I'll run it after lunch. Normal priority.</v>

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:28.560
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, did someone else speak then? Teams did that underwater noise.</v>

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:33.830
<v Callum Reid>Only me. Apparently my finest radio voice isn't getting through.</v>

00:02:34.169 --> 00:02:41.169
<v Grace Liu>Um, I'll do a site visit at the water works with the contractor today. That's a whenever-you-get-a-chance one, isn't it?</v>

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:50.139
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, Grace. Today, but whenever you get a chance. No need to put it ahead of the urgent stuff.</v>

00:02:51.699 --> 00:02:53.449
<v Grace Liu>Yep, I'll take that one.</v>

00:02:53.889 --> 00:03:00.539
<v Grace Liu>And I'll update the risk assessment for work on the boiler feed pump. I'll drop everything for that one.</v>

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:05.139
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed, Grace. That's the one that takes precedence.</v>

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:12.189
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, the visit is flexible. The risk assessment isn't something I'm leaving behind the routine bits.</v>

00:03:13.169 --> 00:03:17.719
<v Tomasz Nowak>Understood. Different urgency, even if they're next to each other in the notes.</v>

00:03:18.479 --> 00:03:23.729
<v Aisha Begum>I'll swap the filter on the air dryer today as well. Low priority, that one.</v>

00:03:24.919 --> 00:03:28.770
<v Olumide Adeyemi>The filter itself, yeah? Not rolling the sensor calibration into that?</v>

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:33.629
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, just the filter on the air dryer today. Low priority. Separate job.</v>

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.219
<v Sarah Okafor>Got it, Aisha.</v>

00:03:37.639 --> 00:03:44.639
<v Aisha Begum>For the other one, I'll recalibrate the sensors on the Compressed Air Dryer on the 3rd. No rush on that.</v>

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:51.939
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Right, so that calibration isn't part of today's filter swap. That's where I was getting muddled.</v>

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:56.330
<v Aisha Begum>Exactly. Compressed Air Dryer sensors on the 3rd, no rush.</v>

00:03:58.599 --> 00:04:00.349
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Aisha. Keeping those separate.</v>

00:04:02.129 --> 00:04:10.879
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha, can you investigate the pressure drop on the turbine two water valve first thing tomorrow? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:15.969
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, I'll investigate it first thing tomorrow. Ahead of the other work.</v>

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:22.779
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, that's the production hold-up, not the filter. Sorry, talking over you there.</v>

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:30.399
<v Sarah Okafor>No, worth being clear. The turbine two water valve needs doing first tomorrow because it's holding production up.</v>

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:35.279
<v Aisha Begum>Understood. First thing tomorrow, that gets first place.</v>

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:42.449
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the Main Outfeed Conveyor by Wednesday.</v>

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:48.569
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sarah, that's both the permit to work and the isolation you're taking?</v>

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:56.500
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, both. I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the Main Outfeed Conveyor by Wednesday.</v>

00:04:57.459 --> 00:04:59.910
<v Grace Liu>Okay, clear. Not just the paperwork half.</v>

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:08.350
<v Sarah Okafor>Tom, can you organise the toolbox talk for the team tomorrow at 9:30? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:12.310
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, sorry, was that nine or half nine? It clipped.</v>

00:05:13.829 --> 00:05:15.930
<v Sarah Okafor>Tomorrow at 9:30. Half nine, Tom.</v>

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:24.860
<v Tomasz Nowak>Got you. I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team tomorrow at 9:30. Not an emergency, but I won't let it slip.</v>

00:05:25.279 --> 00:05:28.430
<v Callum Reid>Teams has only eaten the important syllables this morning.</v>

00:05:30.759 --> 00:05:33.209
<v Tomasz Nowak>Very selective. Heard every word about cake.</v>

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:37.029
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Anything we've crossed wires on?</v>

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:41.899
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No, all clear now. Audio's behaving again as well.</v>

00:05:42.569 --> 00:05:46.769
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, same here. I think two microphones were fighting each other earlier.</v>

00:05:47.899 --> 00:05:52.449
<v Jamie Brennan>Most productive fight in this portakabin. Is the cake chocolate, by the way?</v>

00:05:54.839 --> 00:05:58.339
<v Sarah Okafor>It is. And no, that isn't going in the actions.</v>

00:05:59.649 --> 00:06:02.100
<v Grace Liu>Good. We'd only argue about the priority.</v>

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:07.050
<v Sarah Okafor>We absolutely would. Right, thanks everyone. That's us.</v>
